# Exceptions to CI's vulnerability check, which fails on any HIGH or CRITICAL CVE in a library the JAR
# bundles. An entry is for a CVE that cannot be fixed yet, typically one arriving through midpoint-schema
# that only a new midPoint release removes, and that does not reach midgie's use of the library.
#
# Every entry carries an expiry date, at most 90 days out, and the reason on the line above it. Once the
# date has passed, Trivy no longer honours the entry and the check fails again, so the exception is
# either renewed on purpose or the CVE is gone. Format:
#
#   # <library> <version>, from midpoint-schema <version>: <why midgie is not exposed>.
#   # Gone with midPoint <the release that fixes it>.
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
